<title>UK: City Index opens book on Woolwich B/S.</title>
<headline>City Index opens book on Woolwich B/S.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>City Index has opened a spread betting book on the Woolwich Building Society's closing price on the day of its flotation, the British bookmaker said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>City Index's opening quote was 327 pence stg bid, 337p offered.</p>
<p>The Woolwich is being floated on Monday, July 7. Around 2.5 million members will receive a minimum of 250 free shares from among the 1.6 billion being listed.</p>
<p>City Index's mid-price would give the Woolwich a market capitalisation of around 5.3 billion stg, a level which will see it easily qualify for inclusion in the key FTSE-100 index when it is next revised, due in September.</p>
<p>City Index is a unit of Intercapital Group, a derivatives broker.</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
